# Resume & PDF workflow

## Source of truth

- **`src/data/resume.ts`** is the only content source (experience, summary variants, skills, education, etc.).
- Edit resume content there. Do not duplicate job bullets or summaries elsewhere.
- **`src/data/print-resume.ts`** only *reshapes* that data for PDFs (shorter dates, earlier-role one-liners, bullet caps, layout-oriented structures). Prefer transforming existing fields over inventing new prose.

## Site vs PDF

| Surface | Routes | Layout |
|---|---|---|
| Public site (rich) | `/`, `/web3` | `ResumePage` + resume components |
| PDF template (compact) | `/print`, `/print/web3` | `PrintLayout` + `PrintResume` |

- Summary variant: `general` on `/` and `/print`; `web3` on `/web3` and `/print/web3`.
- `/print*` is for PDF generation only (`noindex`, excluded from sitemap). Do not link it in the public UI or document it as a visitor feature.
- Site and PDF may differ in *presentation* (density, one-liners, skills layout). Shared facts (roles, companies, dates, merged Imaweb block) stay in `resume.ts`.

## After content changes

When experience, summary, skills, or other resume facts change in a way that should appear in application PDFs:

1. Update `src/data/resume.ts` (and `print-resume.ts` only if the reshape logic must change).
2. Run `pnpm pdf` to regenerate `public/CV_MJM_full-stack.pdf` and `public/CV_MJM_web3.pdf`.
3. Include the regenerated PDFs in the same change set when shipping content updates.

Download buttons serve those static files by variant (`resumePdfs` in `resume.ts`), not live print of the public pages.
